#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# factor_terms_list

#% text
# `factor_terms_list(p)` gives the list `[c, q]`: the integer content `c` of the polynomial `p` and the primitive polynomial `q`. `factor_terms_list(p, x)` also splits off the factor free of `x`: `[c, g, q]`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
factor_terms_list(2*x^2 - 2)
#% output
#= [2, -1 + x^2]

#% cell
factor_terms_list(6*a^2 + 9*x^2 + 12*b^2)
#% output
#= [3, 2*a^2 + 3*x^2 + 4*b^2]

#% cell
factor_terms_list(3 + 3*a + 6*a*x + 6*x + 12*a*x^2 + 12*x^2, x)
#% output
#= [3, 1 + a, 1 + 2*x + 4*x^2]

#% section
# See also

